#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "An approach to fault tolerance {#an-approach-to-fault-tolerance}"
msgstr ""
"Pendekatan terhadap toleransi kesalahan {#an-approach-to-fault-tolerance}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll begin by outlining a basic approach to fault-tolerant quantum "
"computing based on quantum circuits and error correcting codes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan mulai dengan menguraikan pendekatan dasar terhadap komputasi "
"kuantum toleran terhadap kesalahan berdasarkan Circuit kuantum dan kode "
"koreksi kesalahan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the sake of this discussion, let us consider the following example of a quantum circuit.\n"
"This happens to be a teleportation circuit, including the preparation of the e-bit, but the specific functionality of the circuit is immaterial — it's just an example, and in actuality we're likely to be interested in significantly larger circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Demi diskusi ini, mari kita pertimbangkan contoh Circuit kuantum berikut.\n"
"Ini kebetulan adalah Circuit teleportasi, termasuk persiapan e-bit, tetapi fungsionalitas spesifik Circuit tidak penting — ini hanya contoh, dan sebenarnya kita kemungkinan tertarik pada Circuit yang jauh lebih besar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A teleportation circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-"
"error-correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/teleportation-"
"circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A teleportation circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-"
"error-correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/teleportation-"
"circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A circuit like this one represents an ideal, and an actual implementation of it won't be perfect.\n"
"So what could go wrong?\n"
msgstr ""
"Circuit seperti ini merepresentasikan ideal, dan implementasi aktualnya tidak akan sempurna.\n"
"Jadi apa yang bisa salah?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fact of the matter is that quite a lot could go wrong!\n"
"In particular, the state initializations, unitary operations, and measurements will all be imperfect;\n"
"and the qubits themselves will be susceptible to noise, including decoherence, at every point in the computation, even when no operations are being performed on them and they're simply storing quantum information.\n"
"That is to say, just about everything could go wrong.\n"
msgstr ""
"Faktanya adalah bahwa cukup banyak yang bisa salah!\n"
"Khususnya, inisialisasi keadaan, operasi uniter, dan pengukuran semuanya akan tidak sempurna;\n"
"dan qubit itu sendiri akan rentan terhadap noise, termasuk dekoherensi, di setiap titik dalam komputasi, bahkan ketika tidak ada operasi yang dilakukan padanya dan mereka hanya menyimpan informasi kuantum.\n"
"Artinya, hampir segalanya bisa salah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is one exception, though: Any *classical* computations that are involved are assumed to be perfect — because, practically speaking, classical computations are perfect.\n"
"For example, if we decide to use a surface code for error correction, and a classical perfect matching algorithm is run to compute corrections, we really don't need to concern ourselves with the possibility that errors in this classical computation will lead to a faulty solution.\n"
"As another example, quantum computations often necessitate classical pre- and post-processing, and these classical computations can safely be assumed to be perfect as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"Namun ada satu pengecualian: komputasi *klasik* mana pun yang terlibat diasumsikan sempurna — karena secara praktis, komputasi klasik memang sempurna.\n"
"Misalnya, jika kita memutuskan untuk menggunakan kode permukaan untuk koreksi kesalahan, dan algoritma pencocokan sempurna klasik dijalankan untuk menghitung koreksi, kita benar-benar tidak perlu mengkhawatirkan kemungkinan bahwa kesalahan dalam komputasi klasik ini akan menghasilkan solusi yang salah.\n"
"Sebagai contoh lain, komputasi kuantum sering memerlukan pra- dan pasca-pemrosesan klasik, dan komputasi klasik ini bisa dengan aman diasumsikan sempurna juga.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Noise models {#noise-models}"
msgstr "Model noise {#noise-models}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze fault-tolerant implementations of quantum circuits, we require a precise mathematical model — a *noise model* — through which *probabilities* for various things to go wrong can be associated.\n"
"Hypothetically speaking, one could attempt to come up with a highly detailed, complicated noise model that aims to reflect the reality of what happens in a particular device.\n"
"But, if the noise model is too complicated or difficult to reason about, it will likely be of limited use.\n"
"For this reason, simpler noise models are much more typically considered.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menganalisis implementasi toleran terhadap kesalahan dari Circuit kuantum, kita memerlukan model matematis yang tepat — *model noise* — melalui mana *probabilitas* untuk berbagai hal yang bisa salah bisa diasosiasikan.\n"
"Secara hipotetis, seseorang bisa mencoba menghasilkan model noise yang sangat detail dan rumit yang bertujuan mencerminkan realitas dari apa yang terjadi di perangkat tertentu.\n"
"Namun, jika model noise terlalu rumit atau sulit untuk dianalisis, kemungkinan besar akan memiliki kegunaan yang terbatas.\n"
"Untuk alasan ini, model noise yang lebih sederhana jauh lebih sering dipertimbangkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One example of a simple noise model is the *independent stochastic noise model*, where errors or faults affecting different components at different moments in time — or, in other words, different *locations* in a quantum circuit — are assumed to be independent.\n"
"For instance, each gate might fail with a certain probability, an error might strike each stored qubit per unit time\n"
"with a different probability, and so on, with *no correlations* among the different possible errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Salah satu contoh model noise sederhana adalah *model noise stokastik independen*, di mana kesalahan atau kerusakan yang mempengaruhi komponen berbeda pada momen berbeda — atau, dengan kata lain, *lokasi* berbeda dalam Circuit kuantum — diasumsikan independen.\n"
"Misalnya, setiap gate mungkin gagal dengan probabilitas tertentu, kesalahan mungkin melanda setiap qubit yang disimpan per satuan waktu\n"
"dengan probabilitas yang berbeda, dan seterusnya, *tanpa korelasi* di antara berbagai kemungkinan kesalahan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, it is certainly reasonable to object to such a model, because there probably will be correlations among errors in real physical devices.\n"
"For instance, there might be a small chance of a catastrophic error that wipes out all the qubits at once.\n"
"Perhaps more likely, there could be errors that are localized but that nevertheless affect multiple components in a quantum computer.\n"
"Nobody suggests otherwise!\n"
"Nevertheless, the independent stochastic noise model does provide a simple baseline that captures the idea that nature is unpredictable but not malicious, and it isn't intentionally trying to ruin quantum computations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, sangat wajar untuk menolak model tersebut, karena mungkin akan ada korelasi di antara kesalahan dalam perangkat fisik nyata.\n"
"Misalnya, mungkin ada sedikit kemungkinan kesalahan katastrofik yang menghapus semua qubit sekaligus.\n"
"Mungkin lebih mungkin, ada kesalahan yang terlokalisir tetapi tetap mempengaruhi beberapa komponen dalam komputer kuantum.\n"
"Tidak ada yang menyarankan sebaliknya!\n"
"Namun demikian, model noise stokastik independen menyediakan dasar sederhana yang menangkap gagasan bahwa alam tidak terduga tetapi tidak jahat, dan tidak dengan sengaja mencoba merusak komputasi kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Other, less forgiving noise models are also commonly studied.\n"
"For example, a common relaxation of the assumption of independence among errors affecting different locations in a quantum circuit is that *just the locations* of the errors are independent, but the actual errors affecting these locations could be correlated.\n"
msgstr ""
"Model noise lain yang kurang toleran juga umum dipelajari.\n"
"Misalnya, relaksasi umum dari asumsi independensi di antara kesalahan yang mempengaruhi lokasi berbeda dalam Circuit kuantum adalah bahwa *hanya lokasi* kesalahan yang independen, tetapi kesalahan aktual yang mempengaruhi lokasi ini bisa berkorelasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Regardless of what noise model is chosen, it should be recognized that "
"*learning* about the errors that affect specific devices, and formulating "
"new error models if the old ones lead us astray, could potentially be an "
"important part of the development of fault-tolerant quantum computation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terlepas dari model noise apa yang dipilih, harus diakui bahwa *mempelajari*"
" kesalahan yang mempengaruhi perangkat tertentu, dan merumuskan model "
"kesalahan baru jika yang lama menyesatkan kita, berpotensi menjadi bagian "
"penting dari pengembangan komputasi kuantum toleran terhadap kesalahan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fault-tolerant circuit implementations {#fault-tolerant-circuit-"
"implementations}"
msgstr ""
"Implementasi Circuit toleran terhadap kesalahan {#fault-tolerant-circuit-"
"implementations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we'll consider a basic strategy for fault-tolerant implementations of quantum circuits.\n"
"We'll use the teleportation circuit above as a running example to illustrate the strategy, though it could be applied to any quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya kita akan mempertimbangkan strategi dasar untuk implementasi Circuit kuantum yang toleran terhadap kesalahan.\n"
"Kita akan menggunakan Circuit teleportasi di atas sebagai contoh yang terus berjalan untuk mengilustrasikan strategi, meskipun ini bisa diterapkan ke Circuit kuantum mana pun.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a diagram of a fault-tolerant implementation of our teleportation "
"circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah diagram implementasi toleran terhadap kesalahan dari Circuit "
"teleportasi kita.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fault-tolerant implementation of a teleportation "
"circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/FT-teleportation-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Fault-tolerant implementation of a teleportation "
"circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/fault-tolerant-quantum-computing/FT-teleportation-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The individual components in this diagram and their connection to the "
"original circuit are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Komponen individual dalam diagram ini dan hubungannya dengan Circuit asli "
"adalah sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"State preparations, unitary gates, and measurements are not performed "
"directly, as single operations, but rather are performed by so-called "
"*gadgets*, which could each involve multiple qubits and multiple operations."
" In the diagram, gadgets are indicated by purple boxes labelled by whatever "
"state preparation, gate, or measurement is to be implemented.\n"
msgstr ""
"Persiapan keadaan, gate uniter, dan pengukuran tidak dilakukan secara "
"langsung, sebagai operasi tunggal, tetapi dilakukan oleh apa yang disebut "
"*gadget*, yang masing-masing bisa melibatkan beberapa qubit dan beberapa "
"operasi. Dalam diagram, gadget ditunjukkan oleh kotak ungu berlabel apa pun "
"persiapan keadaan, gate, atau pengukuran yang akan diimplementasikan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The *logical* qubits on which the original, ideal circuit is run are "
"protected using a quantum error correcting code. Rather than acting directly"
" on these logical qubits, the gadgets act on the *physical* qubits that "
"encode them. The diagram suggests that five physical qubits are used for "
"each logical qubit, as if the $5$-qubit code were being used, but the number"
" could naturally be different. It is worth stressing that these logical "
"qubits are *never* exposed; they spend their entire existence being "
"protected by whatever quantum error correcting code we've chosen.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qubit *logis* tempat Circuit asli yang ideal dijalankan dilindungi "
"menggunakan kode koreksi kesalahan kuantum. Daripada bertindak langsung pada"
" qubit logis ini, gadget bertindak pada qubit *fisik* yang meng-encode-nya. "
"Diagram menyarankan bahwa lima qubit fisik digunakan untuk setiap qubit "
"logis, seolah-olah kode $5$-Qubit sedang digunakan, tetapi jumlahnya tentu "
"saja bisa berbeda. Perlu ditekankan bahwa qubit logis ini *tidak pernah* "
"terekspos; mereka menghabiskan seluruh keberadaannya dilindungi oleh kode "
"koreksi kesalahan kuantum mana pun yang kita pilih.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Error correction is performed repeatedly, as suggested by the blue boxes "
"labeled \"EC\" in the diagram, throughout the computation. It is critically "
"important that this is done both frequently and in parallel. As errors take "
"place, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Entropy is a measure of randomness, "
"uncertainty, or disorder in a system.\">entropy</DefinitionTooltip> builds "
"up, and constant work is required to remove it from the system at a high "
"enough rate to allow the computation to function correctly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Koreksi kesalahan dilakukan berulang kali, seperti yang disarankan oleh "
"kotak biru berlabel \"EC\" dalam diagram, sepanjang komputasi. Sangat "
"penting bahwa ini dilakukan baik secara sering maupun secara paralel. Saat "
"kesalahan terjadi, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Entropy is a measure of "
"randomness, uncertainty, or disorder in a "
"system.\">entropi</DefinitionTooltip> menumpuk, dan pekerjaan konstan "
"diperlukan untuk mengeluarkannya dari sistem dengan kecepatan yang cukup "
"tinggi untuk memungkinkan komputasi berfungsi dengan benar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are therefore specific choices that must be made, including the selection of the gadgets as well as the quantum error correcting code itself.\n"
"Once these choices have been made, and assuming a particular noise model has been adopted, there is a fundamental question that we may ask ourselves:\n"
"Is this actually helping?\n"
"That is, are we making things better, or might we actually be making things worse?\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh karena itu ada pilihan khusus yang harus dibuat, termasuk pemilihan gadget serta kode koreksi kesalahan kuantum itu sendiri.\n"
"Setelah pilihan-pilihan ini dibuat, dan dengan mengasumsikan model noise tertentu telah diadopsi, ada pertanyaan fundamental yang bisa kita ajukan kepada diri sendiri:\n"
"Apakah ini benar-benar membantu?\n"
"Artinya, apakah kita membuat segalanya lebih baik, atau mungkin sebenarnya memperburuk segalanya?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the rate of noise is too high, the entire process just suggested could very well be making things worse, just like the 9-qubit Shor code makes things worse for independent errors if the error probability on each qubit is above the break-even point.\n"
"If, however, the rate of noise is below a certain threshold, then all of this extra work will get us somewhere — and as we'll discuss toward the end of the lesson, paths open up for further error reduction.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika tingkat noise terlalu tinggi, seluruh proses yang baru saja disarankan sangat mungkin memperburuk segalanya, sama seperti kode Shor 9-Qubit memperburuk keadaan untuk kesalahan independen jika probabilitas kesalahan pada setiap qubit di atas titik impas.\n"
"Namun, jika tingkat noise berada di bawah ambang tertentu, maka semua pekerjaan ekstra ini akan membawa kita ke suatu tempat — dan seperti yang akan kita bahas menjelang akhir pelajaran, jalan terbuka untuk pengurangan kesalahan lebih lanjut.\n"
